## Workflow Kit Foundation State

This repository is the **Playwright AI Workflow Kit** — a reusable AI-assisted workflow kit and starter foundation for Playwright automation projects.

npm package name:

- `playwright-ai-workflow-kit`

GitHub repository:

- https://github.com/Avngrss/playwright-ai-workflow-kit

Root documentation entry point:

- `README.md` — kit overview and quick start
- `docs/README.md` — documentation index (which file to open)

User-facing docs:

- `docs/getting-started.md` — clone, install, env, scripts
- `docs/quick-flow.md` — typical feature (plan → API/UI → review)
- `docs/long-flow.md` — extra-command menu: TMS, collections, audit, later extras, E2E, heal
- `docs/commands.md` — slash-command templates
- `docs/prompts.md` — prompt templates

The clean starter baseline intentionally has **no project implementation layer** under `src/test/`.

Skills and commands create the required `src/test/**` structure when implementation starts on a concrete application.

The clean starter baseline also intentionally ships with no `src/test/data/**` data layer.

Create `src/test/data/**` per project only when reusable generated data is actually needed.

Expected project implementation locations (created per application; **absent in clean baseline**):

- `src/test/pages/**` — Page Objects
- `src/test/components/**` — Component Objects
- `src/test/fixtures/**` — fixture chain (`base` -> `api` -> `pages` -> `test.ts`)
- `src/test/setup/auth/**` — auth precondition helpers (disposable user setup)
- `src/test/assertions/**` — assertion helpers (API and UI)
- `src/test/schemas/**` — API Zod schemas
- `src/test/data/**` — builders, generators, datasets
- `src/test/reporting/**` — Allure and reporting helpers
- `src/test/api/clients/**` — thin API clients (when justified)
- `src/test/assets/files/**` — safe synthetic upload assets

Current spec locations (group by feature, never dump specs at the layer root):

- `tests/` — test specs root
- `tests/api/<feature>/` — API specs (`*.api.spec.ts`)
- `tests/ui/<feature>/` — UI specs (`*.ui.spec.ts`)
- `tests/e2e/<area>/` — E2E specs (`*.e2e.spec.ts`)
- `specs/` — feature coverage plans (`specs/<feature>/<feature>.md`)
- `specs/e2e/<area>/` — E2E journey plans (`specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md`)

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/spec-feature-placement.rules.mdc`

Required examples:

- `tests/ui/contact/contact.ui.spec.ts`
- `tests/api/contact/contact.api.spec.ts`
- `tests/e2e/auth/registration-to-login.e2e.spec.ts`

Forbidden:

- `tests/ui/contact.ui.spec.ts`
- `tests/api/login.api.spec.ts`

Quality gate:

- `npm run qa:gate` — convention checks plus `tsc --noEmit`

Package scripts (baseline-safe; all use `--pass-with-no-tests` so zero tests is valid):

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `npm test` | Baseline run: `api` + `ui-chromium` + `e2e` |
| `npm run test:list` | List discovered tests without executing them |
| `npm run test:api` | Run API project (`api`) |
| `npm run test:ui` | Run UI project (`ui-chromium`) |
| `npm run test:e2e` | Run E2E project (`e2e`) |
| `npm run test:smoke` | Baseline `@smoke` run on `api` + `ui-chromium` + `e2e` |
| `npm run test:regression` | Baseline `@regression` run on `api` + `ui-chromium` + `e2e` |
| `npm run test:visual` | Baseline `@visual` run on `ui-chromium` |
| `npm run test:cross-browser` | Run `@cross-browser` on UI browser projects: `ui-chromium`, `ui-firefox`, `ui-webkit` |
| `npm run test:responsive` | Run `@responsive` on `ui-mobile-chromium` |
| `npm run report:allure:generate` | Clean `reports/allure/html/`, then generate from `reports/allure/results/` |
| `npm run report:allure:serve` | Clean HTML, generate, and open Allure report |
| `npm run test:report` | Run baseline tests, then generate and open fresh Allure report |
| `npm run report:allure:clean` | Remove stale Allure results and HTML artifacts |

Rules:

- scripts do not assume project-specific tests, specs, or `src/test/**` exist;
- `npm test` is baseline scope only (`api`, `ui-chromium`, `e2e`) and does not run a full browser/mobile matrix;
- layer scripts use `api`, `ui-chromium`, and `e2e` as default execution projects;
- smoke/regression/visual scripts are baseline-scoped tag runs;
- `test:cross-browser` runs only `ui-chromium`, `ui-firefox`, and `ui-webkit` with `@cross-browser`;
- `test:responsive` runs only `ui-mobile-chromium` with `@responsive`;
- browser and viewport execution still depends on Playwright project configuration in `playwright.config.ts`;
- do not use browser/device tags such as `@firefox`, `@webkit`, `@chromium`, `@mobile`, `@tablet`, or `@desktop`.

First real project tests are created through planning and implementation commands (`/plan-feature`, `/plan-e2e-journey`, `/implement-api-batch`, `/implement-ui-batch`, `/implement-e2e-flow`) — not shipped with the starter baseline.

Starter CI baseline (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`):

- enables npm dependency caching via `actions/setup-node` (`cache: npm`);
- always runs `npm ci`, `npm run qa:gate`, and `npm run test:list`;
- detects whether any `tests/**/*.spec.ts` or `tests/**/*.test.ts` files exist;
- skips matrix test jobs when no tests exist (clean starter still passes);
- maps starter compatibility variables to Playwright env when matrix jobs run (`UI_BASE_URL`, `API_BASE_URL`; empty fallback when unset);
- does not require configured variables or secrets in zero-test state;
- runs API/UI/E2E/tag-based jobs when tests exist;
- includes focused cross-browser UI jobs and responsive mobile UI job via registered projects and coverage-type tags;
- uploads artifacts when generated: `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`, `reports/allure/results/`, `reports/allure/html/`;
- generates Allure HTML report via `npm run report:allure:generate` when `reports/allure/results/` exists after test runs;
- does not configure TMS result publishing;
- does not configure GitHub Pages publishing.

Coverage audit (review only; does not implement tests):

- skill: `.cursor/skills/audit-test-coverage/SKILL.md`
- command: `/audit-test-coverage`
- compares feature plans (`specs/<feature>/<feature>.md`), E2E journey plans (`specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md`), implemented tests, optional TMS mappings, and project map conventions
- use after planning/implementation batches or before cleanup or baseline conversion
- reports missing ready coverage, unplanned tests, duplicate/wrong-layer coverage, blocked/postponed violations, TMS gaps, tag issues, and stale coverage-tied artifacts
- does not modify files, implement tests, delete tests, update TMS, or publish results unless explicitly requested in the same task

Test data strategy audit (review only; does not create or modify data):

- skill: `.cursor/skills/audit-test-data-strategy/SKILL.md`
- command: `/audit-test-data-strategy`
- assesses data safety and maintainability across feature plans, E2E journey plans, specs, `src/test/data/**`, fixtures, and related setup
- use before E2E implementation, before destructive flows, before cleanup or baseline conversion, or when shared mutable data is suspected
- detects shared mutable data, missing isolation/cleanup, inline random data, builder/generator/fixture misuse, E2E data policy gaps, and environment/service ownership issues
- does not modify files, create builders, change tests, delete data, mutate environment, update TMS, or infer cleanup without evidence unless explicitly requested
- for implementation after audit, use `/create-test-data-builder`, `/create-fixture`, `/plan-e2e-journey`, or heal skills as appropriate

Rule references:

- `.cursor/rules/fixtures-data.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/test-data-generation.rules.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/test-isolation-state.rules.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/multi-target-environment.rules.mdc`

Test data generation policy (starter baseline):

- clean starter does not ship `src/test/data/**`;
- create `src/test/data/builders/**`, `src/test/data/datasets/**`, and `src/test/data/generators/**` only when a concrete project needs reusable generated data;
- do not use inline random or faker calls directly in specs;
- do not duplicate reusable payloads, form objects, or shared constants across specs or setup helpers;
- when the same entity exists in API and UI layers, use separate builders per layer and shared datasets for neutral constants such as passwords and dates;
- setup helpers under `src/test/setup/**` must consume builders instead of owning parallel default payloads;
- `@faker-js/faker` is optional and project-driven, not installed by default.

Stability audit (review only; does not heal tests):

- skill: `.cursor/skills/audit-test-stability/SKILL.md`
- command: `/audit-test-stability`
- audits `tests/ui/**`, `tests/e2e/**`, and referenced Page Objects, fixtures, and assertion helpers for flaky patterns
- use after UI/E2E implementation or before committing test changes; optional after failed runs when static review may reveal root cause
- detects forbidden waits, retry anti-patterns, weak assertions, synchronization issues, hidden flows, debug artifacts, data instability, environment/config workarounds, and E2E-specific stability risks
- does not modify files, fix tests, add waits/retries, weaken assertions, install browsers, or run broad suites unless explicitly requested
- for actual fixes, use `/heal-ui-test` or `/heal-api-test`

Rule reference:

- `.cursor/rules/flakiness-policy.rules.mdc`

