## Environment Variables

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/multi-target-environment.rules.mdc`

### Feature Targets / URL Model

The project map is the source of truth for every registered target environment name.

- simple projects: `UI_BASE_URL` and `API_BASE_URL`;
- multi-target projects: register named UI/application, API/service, and external/partner URLs;
- feature plans select only the targets used by that feature;
- setup and cleanup are optional roles using registered targets, not a global precondition URL;
- do not invent target names or derive API hosts from UI hosts.

Framework env template:

- `.env.example` — provider-agnostic placeholders only; safe to commit
- `.env` — local values only; never commit

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` locally and fill placeholders when needed.

### Feature Targets / simple baseline model

Single-application projects may use:

```text
UI_BASE_URL = UI/application target for browser tests and plans

API_BASE_URL = API project/tests base URL
```

Rules:

- API tests use `API_BASE_URL`;
- UI and E2E browser tests use the application target from the feature or journey plan;
- each feature lists only its Feature Targets: UI/application, API/service, external/partner, and setup/cleanup when relevant;
- specs must not read environment variables directly;
- specs must not derive API host from UI host;
- config/env access belongs in approved config or fixture layer.

Do not hardcode product URLs in the starter baseline. Set values in local `.env` or GitHub Variables (CI) for each concrete project.

Example shape only (placeholders — not real URLs):

```text
UI_BASE_URL=https://your-app-host.example
API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example
```

### Multi-target env model

Real projects with multiple UI applications, microfrontends, or API/microservices must extend env ownership here before use.

This project map is the **source of truth** for app and service env names.

Examples only — register actual names per concrete project:

```text
CUSTOMER_APP_URL = customer-facing UI app
ADMIN_APP_URL = admin UI app
CHECKOUT_APP_URL = checkout UI app or microfrontend

AUTH_API_URL = authentication service
USERS_API_URL = user service
ORDERS_API_URL = order service
PAYMENTS_API_URL = payment service
EXTERNAL_PARTNER_API_URL = external or partner system (example logical alias: payment-provider)
```

Register actual env names here before use. Do not copy example names without project-specific registration.

Multi-target rules:

- agents must not invent env variable names;
- feature plans select and document only Feature Targets used: UI/application, API/service, external/partner, and setup/cleanup when relevant;
- E2E journey plans must document every UI app and service crossed;
- do not use generic `API_BASE_URL` when the feature belongs to a specific service;
- do not use a generic application target when the feature belongs to a specific UI app;
- update `.env.example` with commented examples that match registered names;
- there is no global precondition API URL model;
- if a required target is unclear, mark blocked/postponed or request clarification before implementation.

