## Reporting

Reporting integration status:

- Playwright HTML reporter, Allure reporter, and failure artifacts are enabled in `playwright.config.ts`;
- Allure is for local/CI reporting artifacts only — **not** TMS result publishing;
- TMS reporter/result publishing remains separate and not configured by default;
- GitHub Pages report publishing is not configured;
- CI uploads report folders only when they exist (`hashFiles` guards);
- zero-test starter remains valid — no report folders are required when matrix jobs are skipped.

Playwright reporters (`playwright.config.ts`):

- console: `list`
- HTML: `playwright-report/` (`open: never`)
- Allure: `reports/allure/results/` via `allure-playwright` with `detail: false` (only explicit `test.step` in report)

Failure artifacts (Playwright `use` defaults):

- `screenshot: only-on-failure`
- `trace: retain-on-failure`
- `video: retain-on-failure`

Allure report generation:

- cleanup script: `scripts/clean-allure-artifacts.mjs`
- all Playwright `test*` execution scripts clear `reports/allure/results/` before the run
- script: `npm run report:allure:generate` — clears `reports/allure/html/`, then generates from current `reports/allure/results/` using `reports/allure/allurerc.mjs`
- script: `npm run test:report` — baseline test run plus fresh Allure serve
- CI runs generate only when `reports/allure/results/` exists after test execution; fresh checkout avoids local-style accumulation
- step-level custom Allure screenshots in specs are project-specific and not enabled by default
- do not accumulate stale Allure result files locally; `allure generate` merges every file in results

Runtime artifact folders (gitignored):

- `test-results/` — Playwright run output including failure screenshots/traces/videos
- `playwright-report/` — Playwright HTML report
- `reports/allure/results/` — raw Allure results from test runs
- `reports/allure/html/` — generated Allure HTML report
- `reports/allure/allurerc.mjs` — Allure 3 config (committed; `output`, `hideLabels`, `groupBy: ["layer", "feature", "story"]`)

Allure metadata helper (created per project when Allure metadata is first used):

- `src/test/reporting/allure-metadata.helper.ts` — applies feature, story, suite hierarchy, layer, severity, owner, and domain tags via `allure-js-commons` Runtime API
- specs call `applyAllureMetadata({ ... })` — no `testInfo` argument
- do not import deprecated `{ allure }` from `allure-playwright` in specs or helpers
- the clean starter does not ship this helper; implementation skills create it when needed

Allure configuration skill:

- `.cursor/skills/configure-allure-reporting/SKILL.md`

Rules:

- UI and API specs may use the shared Allure metadata helper when a project creates it;
- specs own concrete Allure metadata values;
- shared reporting helpers own reusable metadata application logic;
- Allure metadata may describe reporting dimensions such as browser/project, viewport, layer, feature, story, component, and coverage type;
- Allure metadata must not replace Playwright tags;
- Page Objects and Components must not use Allure;
- API clients must not use Allure;
- builders and generators must not use Allure;
- attachments must be sanitized;
- secrets, tokens, cookies, passwords, `.env`, and storage state files must never be attached.

Future extension:

- create `src/test/reporting/allure-api-diagnostics.helper.ts` only when sanitized API request/response attachments are required.

