## API

Environment variables:

- `API_BASE_URL` — API project/tests base URL;
- `UI_BASE_URL` — UI/application Feature Target in simple projects;
- named Feature Targets — registered per project for additional UI, API, external, setup, or cleanup use.

API documentation / contract source:

- define in project-specific feature plans at `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md`;
- do not hardcode product API URLs in the starter baseline.

API collection input (optional per project):

- rule: `.cursor/rules/api-collection-integration.rules.mdc`
- curated Bruno collections: `collections/bruno/**`
- collection folder guidance: `collections/bruno/README.md`
- the clean starter ships with no real API collection requests;
- Bruno provides executable request examples and planning/audit input;
- OpenAPI/Swagger remains the API contract source of truth when available;
- `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md` remains the automation source of truth.

Bruno workflows:

- inspect: `.cursor/skills/inspect-api-collection/SKILL.md` / `/inspect-api-collection` — read-only collection inventory and drift review;
- plan: `.cursor/skills/plan-from-api-collection/SKILL.md` / `/plan-from-api-collection` — creates or updates only `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md` when explicitly requested;
- audit: `.cursor/skills/audit-api-collection-coverage/SKILL.md` / `/audit-api-collection-coverage` — read-only collection, plan, and API-test alignment audit;
- do not generate tests directly from collections;
- use OpenAPI/Swagger to resolve contract details when available and report Bruno/OpenAPI drift instead of guessing;
- destructive/stateful collection requests require documented cleanup or isolation before automation.

API specs (when added):

- `tests/api/<feature>/**/*.api.spec.ts`

API Playwright project:

- `api`

Shared schema assertion helper (created per project when API schema validation is implemented):

- `src/test/assertions/api/zod-schema.assertion.ts`

API clients (when added):

- `src/test/api/clients/`

API schemas (when added):

- `src/test/schemas/api/`

API types (when added):

- `src/test/api/types/`

UI precondition setup (when added for a concrete project):

- implement in approved project fixture layers;
- UI specs must not read environment variables directly;
- UI specs must not derive API host from UI host;
- setup must verify only required precondition creation and must not hide the UI action under test.

Rules:

- API tests must use the documented API contract as source of truth;
- API tests must not guess payload fields, status codes, or response fields;
- if the API contract is unclear or incomplete, stop and report missing information;
- API tests use request/response model;
- API tests must not use Page Objects or Component Objects;
- API clients are thin and optional;
- API clients must not contain assertions or Allure usage;
- API specs may use the shared Allure metadata helper.

