## Tag Registry

Rule reference:

- `.cursor/rules/test-structure-and-tags.rules.mdc`

Registered Playwright tags by category:

Layer tags:

- `@api`
- `@ui`
- `@e2e`
- `@visual`

Execution scope tags:

- `@smoke`
- `@regression`

Coverage-type tags:

- `@cross-browser`
- `@responsive`

Tag rules:

- `@cross-browser` and `@responsive` are coverage-type tags, not browser or device tags;
- use `@cross-browser` or `@responsive` only when explicitly planned and the scenario needs that coverage classification;
- browser names must not be used as tags: `@chromium`, `@firefox`, `@webkit`;
- viewport or device names must not be used as tags: `@mobile`, `@tablet`, `@desktop`;
- browser and viewport selection belongs to Playwright projects documented in this project map;
- reporting dimensions such as browser, project, viewport, feature, story, and coverage type may be represented through Allure reporting metadata, not invented Playwright tags;
- Allure metadata must not replace required Playwright layer or execution tags;
- agents must not invent new tags without a project map update.

Feature or domain tags may be added only when registered in this project map or an approved tag registry.

Registered feature/domain tags:

- none in the clean starter
- add a tag here before using it in specs

