## Test Strategy

Rules:

- use the lowest reliable test level;
- do not default to UI tests;
- feature plans must include recommended test level per scenario;
- avoid duplicate coverage across API, UI, schema, visual, and E2E tests;
- E2E is a separate planning layer for critical full user/business journeys, not focused UI functional coverage;
- feature coverage plans do not include E2E.

Planning layers:

```text
specs/<feature>/<feature>.md     = feature coverage (API, UI, schema, visual, not automated)
specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md = E2E journey plans (full user/business flows only)
```

Workflow split:

- new feature: `/plan-feature` -> `/implement-api-batch` -> `/implement-ui-batch` -> `/implement-visual-checkpoint`
- product change: `/update-feature-plan` -> `/implement-api-batch` / `/implement-ui-batch` -> `/heal-*` (technical only) -> `qa:gate`
- E2E workflow: `/plan-e2e-journey` -> `specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md` -> `/implement-e2e-flow specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md` -> `tests/e2e/<area>/*.e2e.spec.ts`

Feature change rule:

- `.cursor/rules/feature-change-lifecycle.rules.mdc`

Skill:

- `.cursor/skills/plan-test-coverage/SKILL.md` (feature coverage only)

