## Framework Starter Boundary

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/framework-starter-boundary.rules.mdc`

Purpose:

- distinguish reusable framework baseline content from project-specific artifacts before cleanup or deletion;
- require audit-before-delete classification for baseline conversion work.

Reusable framework content normally includes:

- `.cursor/rules/**`
- `.cursor/skills/**`
- `.cursor/commands/**`
- `docs/**` when reusable for any project
- package/config/tooling files when generic or reviewed
- safe committed project MCP config with Playwright only
- generic scripts such as `scripts/check-conventions.mjs`

Project-specific artifacts normally include:

- `tests/api/**`, `tests/ui/**`, `tests/e2e/**`
- `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md`, `specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md`
- current-app Page Objects, schemas, assertion helpers, builders, generators, fixtures, and visual baselines
- product-specific project map entries until generalized

Generated/runtime artifacts normally include:

- `.playwright-mcp/**`
- `test-results/**`, `playwright-report/**`, `reports/allure/results/**`, `reports/allure/html/**`
- local secrets, temporary debug scripts, and non-starter IDE MCP config

Cleanup policy:

- audit before deletion;
- classify each file as keep, remove, generated, or unsure;
- do not delete unsure files without user decision;
- do not delete framework docs, rules, skills, or commands;
- do not delete package/config files unless explicitly reviewed;
- do not keep sample tests as framework content unless explicitly marked as templates or examples.

Cleanup report must list removed files, preserved files, unsure files left untouched, verification results, and remaining risks.
